<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy September full range naphtha.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy September full range naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy full range naphtha for delivery in September, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>CPC requires the cargo for September 1-30 delivery on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Kaoshiung. The tender closes on July 23 and is valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last tender CPC bought two naphthenic and aromatic naphtha (N+A) for August delivery at between $193-195 per tonne on a c-and-f basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3093)</p>
</text>
